index f5209a5..698c882 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,18 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+To set a default timeout for a session, pass ``timeout`` when creating it::
+
+    s = requests.Session(timeout=(3.05, 27))
+    r = s.get('https://github.com')
+
+You can change the default at any time by assigning ``s.timeout``. Requests that
+omit ``timeout``, including calls to ``s.send()`` with a prepared request, use the
+current session default. An explicit ``timeout=None`` disables it for that request;
+any other explicit timeout overrides it without changing ``s.timeout``. All
+redirects use the timeout selected for the initial request. Sessions default to
+``timeout=None``, preserving the unlimited wait unless a timeout is configured.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
